From 26bbd7a7bb3c43671bd518571faf5c8177b0c367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Laurent Pinchart <laurent.pinchart@ideasonboard.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:24:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] libcamera: software_isp: Exclude saturated pixels from
 AWB statistics

Saturated pixels skew the per-channel means used by AWB and shift the hue of the image. Accumulate unsaturated pixels only (95% threshold).

Backported to v0.7.2 (on top of the focus statistics) from upstream commit 7ebae537183f (2026-10-29), reviewed by Hans de Goede, Milan Zamazal and Kieran Bingham, tested by Robert Mader.
---
 .../internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h       | 29 ++++++++++----
 src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.cpp             | 14 +++++--
 src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp    | 40 ++++++++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h b/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h
index 09f9e6d..b5395c1 100644
--- a/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h
